    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39573" root="ندأ" body-key="n">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدَأَ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدَاَ</span></b> , <i>He hated</i> a thing: or it is a
mistake for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَذَأَ</span>. (As, S, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدَأَ</span>, (S, K,)
aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدَاَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدْءٌ</span> (TA) <i>He cast</i> flesh-meat
<i>into the fire:</i> (K:) or <i>he buried</i> it, (S, K,) or
a cake of bread, (S,) <i>in hot ashes,</i> (S, K, TA,)
that it might become thoroughly cooked, or
baked. (S.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدَأَ</span>, (K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدْءٌ</span>, (TA,)
<i>He frightened.</i> (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدَأَ</span> <i>He cast</i> a person
<i>upon the ground.</i> (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A5-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدَأَ عَلَيْهِمْ</span> <i>He came
forth upon them.</i> (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A6-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدَأَ المَلَّةَ</span> <i>He made,</i>
or <i>prepared, the kind of fire called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ملّة</span>. (K.)

